course: dictionary
lesson: 6654
title: A nun and her community
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A nun is a woman who has promised to give her life to God. She lives in a religious community called a convent and follows rules of prayer and work each day.
explain: Use the words around «nun» to understand it. «Monks and nuns give their whole lives to prayer and service» tells you they spend their lives praying and helping others. In «vows of poverty», a vow is a serious promise.
explain: The clues in «a convent of nuns» and «Sister Mary» help too. The convent is the place where nuns live together, and Sister is one way people address a nun. To check your meaning, swap in "a woman who promised to serve God" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A nun is a woman who has promised to give her life to God.
fact: A convent is a religious community where nuns live and follow rules of prayer and work.
fact: Nuns take vows, which are serious promises, including poverty, chastity and obedience.
fact: Many nuns teach, nurse or care for poor people.
fact: Buddhist traditions also have nuns, so the word is not only used in one religion.
exercise: «Monks and nuns give their whole lives to prayer and service.» What do nuns give their lives to? | *Prayer and helping others | Travelling to a new country each year | Collecting old coins | She plays sport on a team
exercise: «A convent of nuns» is a phrase. What is a convent? | A large castle on a hill | *A religious community where nuns live | A school for very young children | A shop that sells bread
exercise: Priya says a nun is just a teacher in a long dress. Why is she only partly right? | A nun is a teacher in a short dress | Nuns never teach or care for anyone | *Nuns give their lives to God, and many teach, nurse or care for others | Nuns are the same as doctors
test: «Some nuns wear a long dress and a veil called a habit.» What is a habit? | A bad way of doing something | A kind of prayer book | A small room in a convent | *A long dress and veil worn by nuns
test: «Vows of poverty» uses the word vow. What is a vow? | A type of bread | A loud shout in church | A question asked by a teacher | *A serious promise
exam: «Monks and nuns live in communities devoted to prayer and service.» What does devoted mean here? | Painted in bright colours | *Given over fully to something | Lost and forgotten | Shared out between friends
